  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 341 AM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nThe dry weather pattern remains in guidance on Sunday as high \npressure briefly descends upon the area in the wake of a \nrelatively dry FROPA. Some lingering moisture may be enough for a \nfew coastal showers to develop in the afternoon hours, but so far \nNBM keeps max POPs around 10-15% right along the east coast. \n\nFor early next week, high pressure will have broad control of the \nregion, keeping low POPs in place and winds veering from N/NW to a \nmore NE flow by Tuesday. Meanwhile, global models show a short wave \ntrough feature developing over the SE CONUS, and gradually pushing \ninto northern Florida around the late Tuesday-early Wednesday \ntimeframe. The timing of this feature will continue to be adjusted. \nIn the mean time, will keep following NBM's scenario, having this \nfeature bringing a modest air mass modification for Wednesday \nafternoon and Thursday. Low-lvl moisture intrusion from the Atlantic \nmay be enough to push POPs into the 20-30% range. This scenario will \nalso be adjusted as new guidance becomes available.   \n\nThe latest trend in guidance is also to bring a more pronounced \ntemperature gradient as overall northerly flow develops in the \nwake of the FROPA. Afternoon highs should remain in the upper 70s \nto low 80s by early next week.",
